; bfsodium KECCAK PERMUTE 1600 : the whole of Keccak_f{1600}  FIPS 202 section 3
;
; HAND WRITTEN; Twenty four rounds of theta  rho  pi  chi and iota over a 5 by 5
; state of 64 bit lanes; The first four steps are PASTED  because they are two
; routines of their own  and iota is here because it is one exclusive or and
; because the round constant it wants comes from the table below;
;
; INTERFACE entry=200 exit=0 footprint=0:816
; IO  in:  A{200}  twenty five 64 bit lanes  each little endian
;     out: A{200}  the permutation applied
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x0c7  A{200}   the state  in AND out; lane k at cell 8k
;   @0x0c8:0x223  the frames theta and rho pi chi use; both are pasted at this
;                          file's own zero and both work IN PLACE on the state
;                          above  so a round carries nothing between them; The
;                          cells from @0x224 to @0x26f are spare  and they are
;                          what the two steps gave back when their maps were
;                          packed down against the state
;   @0x270:0x32f  KT{192}  the twenty four round constants  eight bytes each;
;                          the one in hand is ALWAYS the lowest  and the rest
;                          slide down eight cells when it has been spent
;   @0x330        n        twenty four rounds  the loop counter
;
; THE ROUND CONSTANTS ARE FIPS 202's OWN NUMBERS and they are written out as
; plusses rather than derived from the linear feedback register that generates
; them; That is the same choice sha512/hashcore makes for K and for the same
; reason  but it costs far less here: a Keccak round constant has bits only at
; positions one less than a power of two  so only bytes NOUGHT ONE THREE and
; SEVEN of a lane are ever anything but nought  and most of those are 128; The
; table below is twenty four blocks of at most four numbers each  and every
; number is read straight out of the standard;
;
; THERE IS NO INDEX  so the constant in hand is always the lowest eight cells of
; the table and the rest of the table SLIDES DOWN when it is spent; That is the
; conveyor this library uses everywhere in place of an address  and it costs one
; hundred and eighty four byte moves of one cell each per round;
;
; The table is written after the read  so the state arrives before anything else
; is on the tape  and the counter cell is exactly where the table's last block
; leaves the pointer  which is why there is no walk between them;

; read the state little endian  leaving the pointer past it
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>
